{"v":15,"id":"e11","kid":"emma","title":"The Mid-Autumn Festival","zh":"中秋节","level":"A2+","genre":"节日文化","src":"facts","sum":"中秋节在农历八月十五，圆月象征团圆。人们赏月、吃月饼，讲嫦娥奔月的故事；中国的探月工程也以嫦娥命名。","words":292,"paras":[{"t":"If you look up at the sky on the fifteenth day of the eighth month of the Chinese lunar calendar, you will see a big, round, bright moon. This is the night of the Mid-Autumn Festival, one of the most important traditional festivals in China. It usually comes in September or early October.","w":[[0,2,"if",-1],[3,6,"you",-1],[7,11,"look",4],[12,14,"up",4],[15,17,"at",4],[18,21,"the",-1],[22,25,"sky",-1],[26,28,"on",-1],[29,32,"the",-1],[33,42,"fifteenth",-1],[43,46,"day",-1],[47,49,"of",-1],[50,53,"the",-1],[54,60,"eighth",-1],[61,66,"month",-1],[67,69,"of",-1],[70,73,"the",-1],[74,81,"chinese",-1],[82,87,"lunar",1],[88,96,"calendar",1],[98,101,"you",-1],[102,106,"will",-1],[107,110,"see",-1],[111,112,"a",-1],[113,116,"big",-1],[118,123,"round",-1],[125,131,"bright",-1],[132,136,"moon",-1],[138,142,"this",-1],[143,145,"is",-1],[146,149,"the",-1],[150,155,"night",-1],[156,158,"of",-1],[159,162,"the",-1],[163,173,"Mid-Autumn",0],[174,182,"festival",0],[184,187,"one",-1],[188,190,"of",-1],[191,194,"the",-1],[195,199,"most",-1],[200,209,"important",-1],[210,221,"traditional",-1],[222,231,"festivals",-1],[232,234,"in",-1],[235,240,"china",-1],[242,244,"it",-1],[245,252,"usually",-1],[253,258,"comes",-1],[259,261,"in",-1],[262,271,"september",-1],[272,274,"or",-1],[275,280,"early",-1],[281,288,"october",-1]]},{"t":"For Chinese people, a full moon is a symbol of reunion. On this day, families try to come home and spend the evening together. They eat a big dinner, sit outside and enjoy looking at the moon. People who are far from home often feel homesick. A famous poem by Li Bai says, \"I raise my head and look at the bright moon; I lower my head and think of my hometown.\"","w":[[0,3,"for",-1],[4,11,"chinese",-1],[12,18,"people",-1],[20,21,"a",-1],[22,26,"full",2],[27,31,"moon",2],[32,34,"is",-1],[35,36,"a",3],[37,43,"symbol",3],[44,46,"of",3],[47,54,"reunion",-1],[56,58,"on",-1],[59,63,"this",-1],[64,67,"day",-1],[69,77,"families",-1],[78,81,"try",-1],[82,84,"to",-1],[85,89,"come",-1],[90,94,"home",-1],[95,98,"and",-1],[99,104,"spend",-1],[105,108,"the",-1],[109,116,"evening",-1],[117,125,"together",-1],[127,131,"they",-1],[132,135,"eat",-1],[136,137,"a",-1],[138,141,"big",-1],[142,148,"dinner",-1],[150,153,"sit",-1],[154,161,"outside",-1],[162,165,"and",-1],[166,171,"enjoy",-1],[172,179,"looking",-1],[180,182,"at",-1],[183,186,"the",-1],[187,191,"moon",-1],[193,199,"people",-1],[200,203,"who",-1],[204,207,"are",-1],[208,211,"far",5],[212,216,"from",5],[217,221,"home",5],[222,227,"often",-1],[228,232,"feel",-1],[233,241,"homesick",-1],[243,244,"a",-1],[245,251,"famous",-1],[252,256,"poem",-1],[257,259,"by",-1],[260,262,"Li",6],[263,266,"Bai",6],[267,271,"says",-1],[274,275,"i",-1],[276,281,"raise",-1],[282,284,"my",-1],[285,289,"head",-1],[290,293,"and",-1],[294,298,"look",-1],[299,301,"at",-1],[302,305,"the",-1],[306,312,"bright",-1],[313,317,"moon",-1],[319,320,"i",-1],[321,326,"lower",-1],[327,329,"my",-1],[330,334,"head",-1],[335,338,"and",-1],[339,344,"think",7],[345,347,"of",7],[348,350,"my",-1],[351,359,"hometown",-1]]},{"t":"The most famous food of the festival is the mooncake. Mooncakes are round, like the full moon. Traditional mooncakes are filled with sweet bean paste, lotus seed paste or nuts, and some have a salted egg yolk in the middle. Today there are also modern flavors, such as ice cream, chocolate and even coffee. Families often give mooncakes to friends and neighbors as gifts.","w":[[0,3,"the",-1],[4,8,"most",-1],[9,15,"famous",-1],[16,20,"food",-1],[21,23,"of",-1],[24,27,"the",-1],[28,36,"festival",-1],[37,39,"is",-1],[40,43,"the",-1],[44,52,"mooncake",-1],[54,63,"mooncakes",-1],[64,67,"are",-1],[68,73,"round",-1],[75,79,"like",-1],[80,83,"the",-1],[84,88,"full",2],[89,93,"moon",2],[95,106,"traditional",-1],[10